# Token Registry Validation

This rule defines how token references must be validated against `docs/_generated/token-registry.json`.

## Blocking checks

- Every token path referenced in docs/specs must resolve in `docs/_generated/token-registry.json`.
- Token paths are case-sensitive and should match canonical registry keys exactly.
- Dot and slash aliases must resolve deterministically to the same canonical entry.

## Error code contract

Canonical code semantics and blocking policy are centralized in `error-codes.mdc` and `.agents/rules/_manifest.yml` (`checks`).

This rule emits `TOK01`, `TOK02`, `TOK03` for markdown token-reference violations.

The standalone token-ref report (see below) maps these to four buckets:
`unresolved_tokens`, `wrong_format_tokens`, `case_mismatch_tokens`, `deprecated_tokens`.

## Validation

Use the docs validation checks and inspect the emitted TOK* findings for token-reference validation.
